        "text": "All Python files have been successfully created in the current working directory. Here are the files and their purposes:\n\n1. **[SAME-SCENARIO] summarize_text.py** - Calls a hosted LLM to summarize long text.\n2. **[SAME-SCENARIO] extract_json.py** - Calls a hosted LLM to extract structured JSON from text.\n3. **[SAME-SCENARIO] answer_with_context.py** - Calls a hosted LLM to answer a question using provided context.\n4. **[SAME-SCENARIO] stream_completion.py** - Streams partial output tokens from a hosted LLM.\n5. **[HELPER] model_client.py** - Provides local configuration and client helper utilities for Hosted LLM Inference and Model-Family Selection.\n6. **[HELPER] model_models.py** - Defines local request, response, and normalization helpers for Hosted LLM Inference and Model-Family Selection.\n7. **[LATER-STEP] prompt_safety.py** - Checks prompts and generated text for unsafe content.\n8. **[LATER-STEP] result_translate.py** - Translates generated model output.\n9. **[LATER-STEP] output_embedding.py** - Embeds model outputs for clustering or retrieval.\n10. **[LATER-STEP] spoken_brief.py** - Generates a spoken brief from the model output.\n\nEach scored file uses a concrete external provider (Google Cloud AI) and makes that provider identifiable in the code. The local helper files contain configuration loading, payload normalization, or response parsing utilities.",
